title: "collator-selection: don't let `set_invulnerables` empty the collator set"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Fixes #13679. `set_invulnerables` refuses an empty list unless the candidate list alone
      can meet `MinEligibleCollators`, but it checked this before dropping the accounts that
      have no registered session keys. A list made up only of such accounts was therefore
      accepted, and `Invulnerables` became empty, which is the state the check exists to
      prevent. Two sessions later the session validator set was empty too.

      The check now runs on the filtered list, so such a call fails with
      `TooFewEligibleCollators`, just like an empty list.
crates:
  - name: pallet-collator-selection
    bump: patch
